### UC03/UC08 – Cancel Tour Booking (happy path, no reason given)
# Prerequisite: first create a booking with UC01 and copy the returned bookingId below.
# The body is optional — a bare POST is the original UC03 behaviour, still supported.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookings/{{bookingId}}/cancel

### UC03/UC08 – Cancel Tour Booking (happy path, with a reason)
# UC08 added attribution: the cancellation is recorded as cancelledBy = USER, and the
# reason is persisted and carried on the BookingCancelledByUser event.
# Prerequisite: a second freshly created booking, since the one above is already CANCELLED.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookings/{{bookingId}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Travel plans changed"
}

### UC03/UC08 – Cancel with an explicit cancellation time
# cancelledAt is optional; when omitted ClockPort supplies it.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookings/{{bookingId}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cancelledAt": "2026-07-15T09:00:00Z",
  "reason": "Weather forecast looks bad"
}

### UC03/UC08 – Error: blank reason (400)
# CancellationReason rejects blank text: cancelling without a reason is allowed, but
# cancelling with an empty one is not. InvalidBookingRequestException -> 400.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookings/{{bookingId}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "   "
}

### UC03/UC08 – Error: reason over 400 characters (401 chars) (400)
# CancellationReason.MAX_LENGTH is 400. The string below is exactly one over.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookings/{{bookingId}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": ""
}

### UC03/UC08 – Error: malformed bookingId (400)
# UUID.fromString raises IllegalArgumentException in the driver, mapped to 400 by
# BookingExceptionHandler. The path variable is a String all the way to the driver, so
# there is nothing for the web layer to validate.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookings/not-a-uuid/cancel

### UC03/UC08 – Error: booking not found (404)
# A random UUID that does not exist in the system.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookings/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/cancel

### UC03/UC08 – Error: invalid state transition (409)
# Prerequisite: cancel a booking once (happy path above) and attempt to cancel it again.
# Cancelling an already-CANCELLED (or ACTIVE/COMPLETED) booking raises
# InvalidBookingStateException. This also protects the original attribution: a second
# attempt cannot overwrite who cancelled first, or why (UC08 AC-06).
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookings/{{bookingId}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Trying to overwrite the first cancellation"
}
